# Native regression: the composer does not offer a task it cannot deliver.
# suite.json enters an English offline demo before this script.
#
# The demo session has exactly one agent, and it is the pane the reader is in.
# Starting a new assistant is held back by `AGENT_SPAWN_SHIPPED`, and the only
# other target -- an assistant already running elsewhere in the session -- does
# not exist here. So there is nowhere to send a task, and the control that
# would open the assistant strip is absent rather than opening an empty row.
#
# This is the same rule the old task screen broke for a year: it offered
# "Existing assistant" as the default target and only said the target was
# unavailable after the whole task had been written. The strip is built from
# the targets that can actually be delivered to, so when there are none there
# is no strip and no toggle.
wait "role=button text=\"Open quick actions\"" 15000
is hidden "id=\"assignment-toggle\""
is hidden "id=\"assignment-bar-close\""
is hidden "id=\"composer-assignment-chip\""
# The composer is an ordinary composer, addressed to the agent on screen.
is visible "id=\"terminal-composer-input\""
is visible "label=\"Send to agent\""
# Quick actions no longer carries its own entry for this. The control that
# opens the assistant strip lives in the key row, a few points below the sheet
# and visible whenever the composer is, so a second one behind a sheet was a
# choice about which button to press rather than about what to do.
press "role=button text=\"Open quick actions\""
wait text "Quick actions" 10000
is hidden "role=button text=\"Assign a task\""
press "role=button label=\"Close quick actions\" || label=\"Close\""
wait "role=button text=\"Open quick actions\"" 10000
is visible "id=\"terminal-composer-input\""
screenshot "shots/collaboration-composer.png"
